LOCATION:James Earl Jones Theatre, 138 West 48th Street, New York NY 10036
DESCRIPTION:<p>How far would you go to get everything you ever WANTED?<br
  /><br />Texas, 1893 &mdash; Twin sisters Mary and Martha Clarke are on the
  run. As Black women who pass for white and hide in plain sight, they
  straddle a dangerous line between two Americas. When powerful forces close
  in to keep their family from claiming a future of their own, Mary and
  Martha are driven to desperate measures to save their mother and their
  family&rsquo;s legacy. Forced to do the unthinkable in order to survive,
  the sisters fight for self-determination, dignity, and an inheritance long
  denied. Through it all, the Kinfolk, a vibrant chorus of ancestors, guide
  Mary and Martha forward on an odyssey of sisterhood, rebellion, and
  freedom.<br /><br />A soulful and dangerous new Broadway musical inspired
  by a Clarke family story carried for generations, <em>Wanted</em> is the
  epic tale of Mary and Martha: sisters, outlaws, legends. This <em>New York
  Times</em> Critic&rsquo;s Pick has been hailed as &ldquo;thrillingly
  original&rdquo; with an &ldquo;audacious and rollicking story.&rdquo; The
  production stars Grammy&reg; winner Ledisi as Tallulah Clarke, Grammy
  nominee Luke James as Elijah, Bradley Jaden as Jesse, and Solea Pfeiffer
  and Liisi LaFontaine as Mary and Martha Clarke.<br /><br /><em>Wanted</em>
  features book and lyrics by <em>Variety</em> &ldquo;Star to Watch&rdquo;
  Angelica Ch&eacute;ri, a descendant of the Sisters Clarke, and music by
  Richard Rodgers Award&ndash;winning composer Ross Baum. The production is
  directed by Tony Award nominee and Obie Award&reg; winner Stevie
  Walker-Webb, with choreography by Chelsey Arce.</p>
END:VEVENT
